+- State the platform guarantee honestly; ordinary Windows containment is a job object, persistent Windows stop is a bounded tree walk, and persistent execution refuses unsupported platforms.
+- Do not add general application approvals or describe prompt guidance, workflow confirmation, or the module execution gate as containment. Ask-mode workflow confirmation is a verified, exactly-once domain decision, not a general tool permission system.
+- Every shell tool refuses recognized writes and deletes outside the project, account data root, registered worktrees, and device sinks, and refuses unplaceable targets before spawning. Cwd never adds a root. Analyzer failure runs the command and emits the coalesced WARN. This static guard is not containment. Plain calls stay outside the file-change records. A persona is read-only when its own definition grants neither the file edit nor the write tool; its shell uses the same analyzer with only scratchpad and device-sink allowances, and refuses `mutates`.
+- A Bash command declared with `mutates` captures only its accepted file-content changes through the shared file edit publisher. A file changed in the project meanwhile is rebased with a three-way merge, never overwritten. Agents run Git repository writes in separate calls without `mutates`. A PATH-first wrapper refuses Git-write modes before execution. A semantic repository backstop runs before any file publication, rejects detected changes without applying files or Git state, and preserves the copy for recovery. Read-only Git remains allowed. The boundary is cooperative; a worktree-only bypass can land. The private copy never publishes Git objects, the index, HEAD, refs, or stash changes. An interrupted current-policy command publishes nothing.
+- One lazy runtime-owned streamed-edit validation worker serves all runners in a generation; it coalesces globally bounded input, captures only closed read-only snapshots, retires exact input and attempt scopes, ignores late results, and is terminated through awaited runtime disposal.
+- Streamed-edit validation is advisory and fail-open: unavailable or retired work never vetoes or delays execution, and final file-tool planning, compare-and-swap publication, verified readback, and settlement remain authoritative.
+- Attribution observes settled file edit publications, including declared Bash edits, without changing, delaying, or replacing tool outcomes.
